    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Broccoli rapini (or broccoli rabe) is a cruciferous green vegetable, related to turnips, not broccoli, known for its distinctly bitter, pungent, nutty flavor from its edible leaves, stems, and small buds, commonly used in Italian cooking, often sautéed with garlic and olive oil to complement its strong taste. </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Grown by: Groundwork Organics in Eugene OR</span></p>",
